n\tpr.Next = snapshoti + 1\n\tpr.sentCommit = snapshoti\n}\n\n// SentEntries updates the progress on the given number of consecutive entries\n// being sent in a MsgApp, with the given total bytes size, appended at log\n// indices >= pr.Next.\n//\n// Must be used with StateProbe or StateReplicate.\nfunc (pr *Progress) SentEntries(entries int, bytes uint64) {\n\tswitch pr.State {\n\tcase StateReplicate:\n\t\tif entries > 0 {\n\t\t\tpr.Next += uint64(entries)\n\tReportUnreachable(id uint64)\n\t// ReportSnapshot reports the status of the sent snapshot. The id is the raft ID of the follower\n\t// who is meant to receive the snapshot, and the status is SnapshotFinish or SnapshotFailure.\n\t// Calling ReportSnapshot with SnapshotFinish is a no-op. But, any failure in applying a\n\t// snapshot (for e.g., while streaming it from leader to follower), should be reported to the\n\t// leader with SnapshotFailure. When leader sends a snapshot to a follower, it pauses any raft\n\t// log probes until the follower can apply the snapshot and advance its state. If the follower\n\t// can't do that, for e.g., due to a crash, it could end up in a limbo, never getting any\n\t// updates from the leader. Therefore, it is crucial that the application ensures that any\n\t// failure in snapshot sending is caught and reported back to the leader; so it can resume raft\n\t// log probing in the follower.\n\tReportSnapshot(id uint64, status SnapshotStatus)\n\t// Stop performs any necessary termination of the Node.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=dict(action='research',rationale='Use the remaining source-work window to retain a concrete snapshot transport/progress discriminator, without starting an execution that lacks a fixed contract.',sources=[dict(id='S_progress_modes',file='tracker/progress.go',start_line=105,end_line=169,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S_progress_pause',file='tracker/progress.go',start_line=255,end_line=273,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S_snapshot_report_contract',file='node.go',start_line=234,end_line=246,kind='interface_statement')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_progress_modes','S_progress_pause','S_snapshot_report_contract','S_leader_other','S_raw_snapshot_report','S_replication_send'],answered='The snapshot-send recovery path separates transport status from replication support. In StateSnapshot, leader MsgSnapStatus success enters Probe with Next=max(Match+1,pendingSnapshot+1); failure first clears PendingSnapshot then enters Probe from Match+1. Both pause MsgApp flow. HeartbeatResp clears the flow pause and can trigger append probing, but IsPaused remains true while still in StateSnapshot. These transitions do not raise Match, so transport success alone is not append-quorum support. The Node ReportSnapshot comment calls SnapshotFinish a no-op, whereas RawNode.ReportSnapshot forwards a non-reject MsgSnapStatus and the leader branch does change progress state. This is a concrete documentation/implementation semantic gap to interpret, not an executed defect.',remaining=['Determine whether no-op means no additional caller obligation or literally no observable retry-state effect; current source wording and implementation behavior should both be retained.','A source-produced snapshot stream failure/success comparison could distinguish retry state from acknowledged replication support, but would need fixed transport failure assumptions and actual control completion.','No general liveness conclusion follows from pause/probe state or the lack of a bounded retry execution.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The next useful local question is whether actual snapshot transport status can prematurely contribute matched support or only reposition a retry probe. Source currently supports the latter mechanism; a check should observe Match and actual follow-up responses independently and avoid treating a permitted pause as a safety failure. Existing snapshot campaign and configuration observations keep their original scope; none relied on ReportSnapshot being literally side-effect-free.'))\njson.dump(p,open('submission-snapshot-transport-handoff.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-snapshot-transport-handoff.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
